{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_4460290131b816bb\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_4460290131b816bb/topic_2\", \"topic_label\": \"Overlapping or background speech affecting transcription\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b\", \"member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that a background speaker gets transcribed as the main speaker.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks how much overlap is allowed before a transcription fails the rubric.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports two seconds of overlap with the rest clear in the background-speaker thread, and reports hearing both voices but losing individual words in the overlap in the rubric-question thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor in each thread asks whether the rest of the recording is intelligible enough to continue; the QA tutor in the background-speaker thread also distinguishes overlap duration from word intelligibility.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"The team lead requests timestamps in both threads so QA can determine whether overlap affects the full sample or only a short segment; in the background-speaker thread, the team lead also says the remainder may still be usable.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied threads contain no timestamps answering the team lead's requests, and the rubric-question thread contains no subsequent answer to the QA tutor's question about the remainder's intelligibility.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ directs marking and timestamping overlapping or unintelligible intervals, preserving the usable remainder, and not inferring a whole-clip failure from a short affected interval.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions direct marking overlapping or unintelligible intervals, keeping usable portions, timestamping the affected span, and distinguishing words missing from the audio from reference-transcript mistakes.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:eb85357a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks how much speaker overlap makes a transcription fail; a separate tutor reports background speech being transcribed as the main speaker.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The team lead has requested timestamps in both threads for QA assessment, and neither supplied thread contains the requested timestamps.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports two seconds of overlap with the rest clear in the background-speaker thread, and audible voices with individual words lost in the overlap in the rubric-question thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the remainder is intelligible in each thread; the rubric-question thread contains no subsequent answer about the remainder.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says to mark and timestamp the affected interval, preserve the usable remainder, and not infer whole-clip failure from a short affected interval.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:no_action\", \"kind\": \"NO_ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why no further action is needed now: The team lead has already requested inputs for QA assessment, consistent with current guidance. Those inputs are still missing, so a further intervention would duplicate the handling already underway.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:eb85357a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead provides the next step and says the remainder may still be usable, but the supplied thread has no requested timestamps or final QA assessment of the reported transcription issue.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead establishes timestamping for QA assessment, but the supplied thread does not answer the tutor's failure-threshold question or provide the requested timestamps and remainder-intelligibility answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: The reports describe localized overlap and a transcription issue, with one tutor describing the remainder as clear. The supplied messages do not establish broader disruption or conflicting scoring decisions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U020\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U020 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U018\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U018 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890932.000133\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b\", \"thread_id\": \"1790890932.000133\", \"author_id\": \"U020\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:42:12.000133Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Background speaker gets transcribed as main speaker.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790890987.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b\", \"thread_id\": \"1790890932.000133\", \"author_id\": \"U018\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:43:07.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The speakers overlap for two seconds, but the rest is clear.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891025.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b\", \"thread_id\": \"1790890932.000133\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:43:45.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the rest of the recording intelligible enough to continue the task? Overlap duration and word intelligibility are separate observations.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790891074.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b224f8f278e4849b8a75936b\", \"thread_id\": \"1790890932.000133\", \"author_id\": \"U006\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:44:34.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Please timestamp the overlap so QA can determine whether it affects the full sample or only a short segment. The remainder may still be usable even if a short segment is unclear.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941015.000132\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22\", \"thread_id\": \"1790941015.000132\", \"author_id\": \"U015\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T11:36:55.000132Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U015\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Could QA clarify this case: How much overlap is allowed before the transcription fails the rubric?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941070.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22\", \"thread_id\": \"1790941015.000132\", \"author_id\": \"U018\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T11:37:50.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U015\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thumbsup\", \"users\": [\"U012\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"I can hear both voices, though individual words in the overlap are lost.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941105.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22\", \"thread_id\": \"1790941015.000132\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T11:38:25.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U015\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the rest of the recording intelligible enough to continue the task?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790941162.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_e48bf44fa3dd5692a771cf22\", \"thread_id\": \"1790941015.000132\", \"author_id\": \"U006\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T11:39:22.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U015\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Please timestamp the overlap so QA can determine whether it affects the full sample or only a short segment.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Scoring\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Scoring\\n\\n### Q: How should I score mild clipping?\\nBrief, localized clipping with clear speech is a minor defect. Timestamp the affected span. For continuous artifacts or unclear impact, ask QA to review intelligibility and scope; do not decide from duration alone.\\n\\n### Q: The transcript and audio disagree. What do I do?\\nRecord the exact mismatch as a correspondence issue. Distinguish a recording error from a reference-transcript error; do not classify the mismatch as a playback failure.\\n\\n### Q: How much speaker overlap is allowed before the transcription fails?\\nMark the overlapping or unintelligible interval and preserve the usable remainder. Timestamp the span. Do not infer a whole-clip failure from a short affected interval.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:eb85357a\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Overlap and transcript correspondence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Overlap and transcript correspondence\\nMark the overlapping or unintelligible interval. Keep usable portions of the clip and timestamp the affected span. Distinguish words missing from the audio from mistakes in the reference transcript.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:6eeb0c96\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Scoring audio quality\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Scoring audio quality\\n- Assess intelligibility and the affected span, not the word “clipping” alone.\\n- Brief, localized clipping or static with speech remaining clear is a minor defect.\\n- An artifact that makes a material speech span unusable is a major defect.\\n- Continuous artifacts or borderline impact require QA review with timestamps and an intelligibility description. Duration alone does not establish a major defect.\\n- Before treating silence as a content issue, verify playback, volume, and whether the audio file itself is silent. Preserve uncertainty when this cannot be checked.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1131a168\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor here describe task-quality defects, not operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Intelligibility | A material speech span is unusable | Brief clipping/static with words still clear | Background variation that does not impair the task |\\n| Audio–transcript correspondence | Key content is missing or contradicted | A limited omission that does not change meaning | Equivalent wording where the task allows it |\\n| Language match | A substantial unrequested mismatch with the required language | A limited genuine mismatch affecting adherence | Permitted switching, ordinary loanwords, or an acceptable accent |\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:f72aa6db\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Language and TTS\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language and TTS\\n\\n### Q: The generated speech is in the wrong language. Is that a playback failure?\\nConfirm the requested language and permitted switching. If the recording itself contains an unrequested language mismatch, record it as a language-quality issue rather than a playback failure.\"}], \"open_review_flag